Package: LibeRties
Type: Package
Title: Portable Job Execution for LibeR
Version: 0.8.1
Authors@R: person("Sven C.", "van Dijkman",
    email = "svdijkman@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Sven C. van Dijkman [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Sven C. van Dijkman <svdijkman@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Executes serialized LibeR simulation and estimation jobs in
    restricted subprocesses, hardened transient systemd user services, or
    resource-managed Slurm and Grid Engine allocations with isolated per-user
    working directories. A persistent cross-platform local
    queue uses background R worker processes and the same versioned job
    contract used by remote Linux servers. Payload checksums, explicit state transitions,
    metadata locking, safe path components, cancellation, logs, restart
    recovery, per-tenant quotas, monitored resource limits, and result
    provenance are built into the contract. Production deployments use the
    native systemd isolation backend or an independently attested scheduler
    sandbox and require TLS termination.
